From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Local <codex-local@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:28:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] Restore native audio through KFIV's original sound
 drivers

Implement SPU2 mixing and the host audio clock/output path, and route the
USA game's remote sound SDK through the existing physical IOP service.
Share CD sector mapping for the original MPEG audio/input pumps, preserve
accepted packet retries, cancel stale callbacks, and account IPU input DMA.
Publish the original SDK's decoder/reference status; recognize committed
program end independently of unread CD padding, without ending on video
sequence markers or parsing packets after program end.

Allow the SDK's priority-zero startup thread and advance wall-due field
events with timer accounting. Register decoded wrapper continuations with
deterministic ownership so movie workers resume through native scheduling.
